BE NOC — Drug Substance Specification (Section 8): extraction + fallback fix

Context: user uploads DRL STP / Test Method docs (STP 167410 Pseudoephedrine,
Test Method 166548 Finished Product). These are METHOD documents (procedures,
chromatographic conditions, calculations) — NOT clean Specification tables. The
current output writes "As per STP No. XXX" for every test and bloats to 15 rows
with duplicates. Fix as follows.

RULE 1 — Extract limits where the STP CONTAINS them; keep the reference where it
does not (never fabricate):
For each spec-table test, search the STP body for an explicit acceptance
criterion / limit. If found, put the ACTUAL limit in the Specifications column.
If the STP only gives a procedure with no limit, keep "As per STP No. XXX" as
the honest fallback (do NOT invent a limit).

For Pseudoephedrine STP 167410 specifically, these limits ARE present and MUST
be extracted (not left as "As per STP"):
- Related Substances / Impurities by HPLC: 1-Ephedrine HCl NMT 0.10%,
Acetylephedrine NMT 0.10%, Benzaldehyde NMT 0.10%, Individual unspecified
NMT 0.10%, Total unspecified NMT 0.20%, Total impurities NMT 0.50%.
- Elemental Impurities (ICP-OES): As 1.5, Hg 3.0, Pb 0.5, Cd 0.5, Co 5,
Ni 10, V 10, Pt 10 (µg/g).
- Ordinary Impurities: NMT 2.0% (total).
These tests have NO limit in the STP → keep "As per STP No. 167410":
Description, Solubility, Sulfate, Melting Range, Specific Rotation, pH,
Loss on Drying, Residue on Ignition, Chloride, Identification.

RULE 2 — De-bloat and de-duplicate the test list:
Collapse duplicate concepts to ONE row:
- "Melting Range" and "Melting Point" → single "Melting Range" row.
- "Elemental Impurity By ICP-OES method" and "Elemental Impurities" →
single "Elemental Impurities" row.
EXCLUDE STP sections that are methods/support, not spec-table tests:
Microbiological Test, Residual Solvents by GC (method), Bulk Density,
Particle Size, Assay(HPLC) duplicate, system-suitability sections.
Result: a clean ~7-test drug-substance spec (matching the approved
main-document Section 10 structure), not 15 rows.

RULE 3 — Distinguish STP vs Specification source, and surface a data-gap note:
An uploaded STP / "Test Method" (procedures) is NOT a Specification document
(clean acceptance-criteria table). When only the STP is available, populate
limits ONLY where the STP contains them (Rule 1) and, for the remaining tests,
keep "As per STP No. XXX". Add a checklist/warning (NOT in the DOCX body):
"Specification document not uploaded for <API>; limits populated only where
present in the STP. Upload the Specification to complete Section 8."

RULE 4 — Missing Loratadine specification:
Section 8.1 Loratadine is empty because the Loratadine STP/Specification was
NOT uploaded (only Pseudoephedrine STP 167410 was). Keep "Not provided." for
Loratadine and flag in checklist: "Loratadine drug-substance STP/Specification
not uploaded." Do NOT create a phantom API section from the dose string
"5mg120mg" (RED FLAG 2 — dose-string API split): strip dose strings before
API-name resolution so no "Pseudoephedrine Sulfate 5mg120mg" phantom appears.

ACCEPTANCE (Pseudoephedrine, STP 167410 uploaded, Specification NOT uploaded):
- Related Substances row(s) show NMT 0.10 / 0.20 / 0.50% actual limits.
- Elemental Impurities row shows As 1.5 / Hg 3.0 / Pb 0.5 / Cd 0.5 / Co 5 /
Ni 10 / V 10 / Pt 10 µg/g.
- Ordinary Impurities row shows NMT 2.0%.
- Description/LOD/ROI/Melting Range/Assay etc. show "As per STP No. 167410"
(no fabricated limits).
- ~7 tests total, no duplicate Melting/Elemental rows, no microbiology/RS-GC
rows.
- Loratadine 8.1 = "Not provided"; no phantom "…5mg120mg" API section.
- Checklist warns: Specification doc missing; Loratadine STP missing.

NON-GOALS: never fabricate a limit not present in an uploaded document; never
drop a limit that IS present; keep "As per STP No. XXX" only as the fallback for
tests genuinely lacking a limit in the source.

